      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the current implementation, yes, only the first 3 fields are used in computing kh_hmac. We could also move the auth_seed and auth_hmac to right after origin_seed, and use everything to compute the kh_hmac; this would solve the other problem you mentioned - we wouldn\u0027t need a U2F_VKH_KEYPAIR_INPUT_LEN or a header struct. It just feels a little strange to use one hmac as the input of another hmac - I don\u0027t know",
      "parentUuid": "2e96588d_6231f8ae",
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
